IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa7-ch7`

-- coa7-ch5.l4: Part 13 Chapter 5, Additional requirements for quoted companies and traded companies (ss 341 to 354),
-- lines 4368-4552 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4. Seams taken as inputs: `s 361` (this part, ch7), `s 1121` (coa24),
-- `s 1162` parent and subsidiary undertakings (keel), `s 153` (coa3).

§ `Part 13 Chapter 5 -- Additional requirements for quoted companies and traded companies`

§§ `Website publication of poll results`

-- ---- s 341 Results of poll to be made available on website -------------------------------------------------

-- src:4371 | (1) Where a poll is taken at a general meeting of a quoted company that is not a traded company, the company must ensure that the following information is made available on a website—
-- src:4372 | (a) the date of the meeting,
-- src:4373 | (b) the text of the resolution or, as the case may be, a description of the subject matter of the poll,
-- src:4374 | (c) the number of votes cast in favour, and
-- src:4375 | (d) the number of votes cast against.
@ref s 341(1) Results of poll to be made available on website: quoted company that is not a traded company (src:4371-4375)
GIVEN `s 361 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a poll is taken at a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the meeting is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes cast in favour is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes cast against is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(1) the quoted company has made the information available on a website` MEANS
    IF `the company is a traded company` OR (NOT `a poll is taken at a general meeting of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a poll is taken at a general meeting of a quoted company that is not a traded company" -- FORK F19
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 361 the company is a quoted company`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a quoted company (s 385) is not known
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a general meeting of a quoted company that is not a traded company"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the date of the meeting is made available on a website`
                 AND `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll is made available on a website`
                 AND `the number of votes cast in favour is made available on a website`
                 AND `the number of votes cast against is made available on a website`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ensure that the following information is made available on a website— (a) the date of the meeting, (b) the text of the resolution or ... a description of the subject matter of the poll, (c) the number of votes cast in favour, and (d) the number of votes cast against" -- FORK F5

-- src:4376 | (1A) Where a poll is taken at a general meeting of a traded company, the company must ensure that the following information is made available on a website—
-- src:4377 | (a) the date of the meeting,
-- src:4378 | (b) the text of the resolution or, as the case may be, a description of the subject matter of the poll,
-- src:4379 | (c) the number of votes validly cast,
-- src:4380 | (d) the proportion of the company's issued share capital (determined at the time at which the right to vote is determined under section 360B(2)) represented by those votes,
-- src:4381 | (e) the number of votes cast in favour,
-- src:4382 | (f) the number of votes cast against, and
-- src:4383 | (g) the number of abstentions (if counted).
@ref s 341(1A) Results of poll to be made available on website: traded company (src:4376-4383)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a poll is taken at a general meeting of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the meeting is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes validly cast is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proportion of the company's issued share capital (determined at the time at which the right to vote is determined under section 360B(2)) represented by those votes is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes cast in favour is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of votes cast against is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `abstentions are counted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of abstentions is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(1A) the traded company has made the information available on a website` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) OR (NOT `a poll is taken at a general meeting of the company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a poll is taken at a general meeting of a traded company"
    ELSE IF `the date of the meeting is made available on a website`
            AND `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll is made available on a website`
            AND `the number of votes validly cast is made available on a website`
            AND `the proportion of the company's issued share capital (determined at the time at which the right to vote is determined under section 360B(2)) represented by those votes is made available on a website`
            AND `the number of votes cast in favour is made available on a website`
            AND `the number of votes cast against is made available on a website`
            AND ((NOT `abstentions are counted`) OR `the number of abstentions is made available on a website`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ensure that the following information is made available on a website— (a) ... (g) the number of abstentions (if counted)" -- FORK F5

-- "(a) the end of 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting": the day of the meeting is the first of the 16 days, so the
-- last day is 15 days after it; "(b) if later, the end of the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll
-- is declared" (that working day is an input).
-- src:4384 | (1B) A traded company must comply with subsection (1A) by—
-- src:4385 | (a) the end of 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting, or
-- src:4386 | (b) if later, the end of the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared.
@ref s 341(1B) Results of poll to be made available on website: time (src:4384-4386)
GIVEN `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the information was made available on a website` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(1B) the traded company has complied with subsection (1A) in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the information was made available on a website`
        AT MOST (IF `the day of the meeting` PLUS 15 AT LEAST `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared`
                 THEN `the day of the meeting` PLUS 15
                 ELSE `the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A traded company must comply with subsection (1A) by— (a) the end of 16 days beginning with the day of the meeting, or (b) if later, the end of the first working day after the day on which the result of the poll is declared" -- FORK F7

-- src:4387 | (2) The provisions of section 353 (requirements as to website availability) apply.
@ref s 341(2) Results of poll to be made available on website: section 353 (src:4387)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of section 353` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(2) the provision of section 353 applies for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a provision of section 353`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of section 353 (requirements as to website availability) apply"

-- src:4388 | (3) In the event of default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 341(3) Results of poll to be made available on website: offence (src:4388)
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company is in default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section), an offence is committed b ..." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4389 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 341(4) Results of poll to be made available on website: penalty (src:4389)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 341(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
-- src:4390 | (5) Failure to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353) does not affect the validity of—
-- src:4391 | (a) the poll, or
-- src:4392 | (b) the resolution or other business (if passed or agreed to) to which the poll relates.
@ref s 341(5) Results of poll to be made available on website: validity (src:4390-4392)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(5) the failure affects the validity of the poll or of the resolution or other business to which the poll relates` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353) does not affect the validity of— (a) the poll, or (b) the resolution or other business (if passed ..."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply

-- src:4393 | (6) This section only applies to polls taken after this section comes into force.
@ref s 341(6) Results of poll to be made available on website: polls before commencement (src:4393)
GIVEN `the poll was taken after this section came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 341(6) this section applies to the poll` MEANS
    IF `the poll was taken after this section came into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section only applies to polls taken after this section comes into force"

§§ `Independent report on poll`

-- ---- s 342 Members' power to require independent report on poll ---------------------------------------------

-- src:4396 | (1) The members of a quoted company may require the directors to obtain an independent report on any poll taken, or to be taken, at a general meeting of the company.
@ref s 342(1) Members' power to require independent report on poll (src:4396)
GIVEN `s 361 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(1) the members may require the directors to obtain an independent report on a poll` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 361 the company is a quoted company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The members of a quoted company may require the directors to obtain an independent report"

-- src:4397 | (2) The directors are required to obtain an independent report if they receive requests to do so from—
-- src:4398 | (a) members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates (excluding any voting rights attached to any shares in the company held as treasury shares), or
-- src:4399 | (b) not less than 100 members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates and hold shares in the company on which there has been paid up an average sum, per member, of not less than £100.
-- src:4400 | See also section 153 (exercise of rights where shares held on behalf of others).
@ref s 342(2) Members' power to require independent report on poll: the requests (src:4397-4400)
GIVEN `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates and hold shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
      `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(2) the directors are required to obtain an independent report` MEANS
    IF `voting rights represented by the requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `total voting rights of all the members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates (excluding treasury shares)`
        OR (`number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates and hold shares in the company` AT LEAST 100
            AND `total sum paid up on the shares those members hold` AT LEAST `number of requesting members who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates and hold shares in the company` TIMES 100)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors are required to obtain an independent report if they receive requests to do so from— (a) members representing not less than 5% of the total voting rights ... or (b) not less than 100 members" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4401 | (3) Where the requests relate to more than one poll, subsection (2) must be satisfied in relation to each of them.
@ref s 342(3) Members' power to require independent report on poll: more than one poll (src:4401)
GIVEN `the requests relate to more than one poll` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each of the polls, subsection (2) is satisfied` IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(3) subsection (2) is satisfied in relation to each poll` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the requests relate to more than one poll`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the requests relate to more than one poll" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF and `for each of the polls, subsection (2) is satisfied`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (2) must be satisfied in relation to each of them"

-- (d) received by the company not later than one week after the date on which the poll is taken (s 360 does not list this).
-- src:4402 | (4) A request—
-- src:4403 | (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form,
-- src:4404 | (b) must identify the poll or polls to which it relates,
-- src:4405 | (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and
-- src:4406 | (d) must be received by the company not later than one week after the date on which the poll is taken.
@ref s 342(4) Members' power to require independent report on poll: the request (src:4402-4406)
GIVEN `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request identifies the poll or polls to which it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the poll is taken` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the company received the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 342(4) the request meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the request is in hard copy form or in electronic form`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A request— (a) may be in hard copy form or in electronic form"
    ELSE IF `the request identifies the poll or polls to which it relates`
            AND `the request is authenticated by the person or persons making it`
            AND `the day on which the company received the request` AT MOST `the date on which the poll is taken` PLUS 7
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) must identify the poll or polls to which it relates, (c) must be authenticated by the person or persons making it, and (d) must be received by the company not later than one week after the date on which the poll is taken" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 343 Appointment of independent assessor -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4408 | (1) Directors who are required under section 342 to obtain an independent report on a poll or polls must appoint a person they consider to be appropriate (an “independent assessor”) to prepare a report for the company on it or them.
@ref s 343(1) Appointment of independent assessor (src:4408)
GIVEN `the directors are required under section 342 to obtain an independent report on a poll or polls` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343(1) the directors must appoint an independent assessor to prepare a report` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the directors are required under section 342 to obtain an independent report on a poll or polls`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Directors who are required under section 342 to obtain an independent report on a poll or polls must appoint a person they consider to be appropriate" -- MARGINAL a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether section 342 requires the report is not known

-- src:4409 | (2) The appointment must be made within one week after the company being required to obtain the report.
@ref s 343(2) Appointment of independent assessor: within one week (src:4409)
GIVEN `the day on which the company became required to obtain the report` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the appointment was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343(2) the appointment was made in time` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the appointment was made` AT MOST `the day on which the company became required to obtain the report` PLUS 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The appointment must be made within one week after the company being required to obtain the report" -- FORK F7

-- src:4410 | (3) The directors must not appoint a person who—
-- src:4411 | (a) does not meet the independence requirement in section 344, or
-- src:4412 | (b) has another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report (including, in particular, a role in connection with collecting or counting votes or with the appointment of proxies).
@ref s 343(3) Appointment of independent assessor: persons who must not be appointed (src:4410-4412)
GIVEN `s 344(1) the person may not be appointed as an independent assessor` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report (including a role in connection with collecting or counting votes or with the appointment of proxies)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343(3) the directors may appoint the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report (including a role in connection with collecting or counting votes or with the appointment of proxies)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must not appoint a person who— ... (b) has another role in relation to any poll on which he is to report"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 344(1) the person may not be appointed as an independent assessor`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors must not appoint a person who— (a) does not meet the independence requirement in section 344"
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a person who meets the independence requirement and has no other role is not forbidden by this subsection, which does not say he may be appointed
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the independence requirement is met is not known

-- src:4413 | (4) In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 343(4) Appointment of independent assessor: offence (src:4413)
GIVEN `the directors are in default in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343(4) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the directors are in default in complying with this section`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4414 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 343(5) Appointment of independent assessor: penalty (src:4414)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 343(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- src:4415 | (6) If at the meeting no poll on which a report is required is taken—
-- src:4416 | (a) the directors are not required to obtain a report from the independent assessor, and
-- src:4417 | (b) his appointment ceases (but without prejudice to any right to be paid for work done before the appointment ceased).
@ref s 343(6) Appointment of independent assessor: no poll taken (src:4415-4417)
GIVEN `no poll on which a report is required is taken at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343(6) the directors are not required to obtain a report and the assessor's appointment ceases` MEANS
    IF `no poll on which a report is required is taken at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at the meeting no poll on which a report is required is taken" -- MARGINAL a

@ref s 343(6)(b) Appointment of independent assessor: payment for work done (src:4417)
GIVEN `the assessor's appointment has ceased under paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 343(6)(b) the cessation prejudices a right to be paid for work done before the appointment ceased` MEANS
    IF `the assessor's appointment has ceased under paragraph (b)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "his appointment ceases (but without prejudice to any right to be paid for work done before the appointment ceased)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "his appointment ceases (but without prejudice"

-- ---- s 344 Independence requirement ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4430 | (2) An auditor of the company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose.
@ref s 344(2) Independence requirement: auditors (src:4430)
GIVEN `the person is an auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is otherwise an officer or employee of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose` MEANS
    IF `the person is an auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An auditor of the company is not regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose"
    ELSE IF `the person is otherwise an officer or employee of the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) an officer or employee of the company" is not what the person is, on the facts given -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4431 | (3) In this section—
-- src:4432 | “associated undertaking” means—
-- src:4433 | (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company, or
-- src:4434 | (b) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company; and
-- src:4435 | “associate” has the meaning given by section 345.
@ref s 344(3) Independence requirement: "associated undertaking" (src:4431-4435)
GIVEN `the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(3) the undertaking is an associated undertaking of the company` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company` OR `the undertaking is a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“associated undertaking” means— (a) a parent undertaking or subsidiary undertaking of the company, or (b) a subsidiary undertaking of a parent undertaking of the company"

-- (a) an officer or employee of the company (an auditor does not count: subsection (2)), or a partner or employee of such a
-- person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner; (b) the same for an associated undertaking; (c) a connection
-- of a description specified by regulations (an input: the regulations are not among the sources).
-- src:4419 | (1) A person may not be appointed as an independent assessor—
-- src:4420 | (a) if he is—
-- src:4421 | (i) an officer or employee of the company, or
-- src:4422 | (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner;
-- src:4423 | (b) if he is—
-- src:4424 | (i) an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company, or
-- src:4425 | (ii) a partner or employee of such a person, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner;
-- src:4426 | (c) if there exists between—
-- src:4427 | (i) the person or an associate of his, and
-- src:4428 | (ii) the company or an associated undertaking of the company,
-- src:4429 | a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 344(1) Independence requirement: who may not be appointed (src:4419-4429)
GIVEN `s 344(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State exists between the person or an associate of his and the company or an associated undertaking of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 344(1) the person may not be appointed as an independent assessor` MEANS
    IF `s 344(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of the company, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
        OR `the person is an officer or employee of an associated undertaking of the company`
        OR `the person is a partner or employee of an officer or employee of an associated undertaking, or a partnership of which such a person is a partner`
        OR `a connection of a description specified by regulations made by the Secretary of State exists between the person or an associate of his and the company or an associated undertaking of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 344(2) the person is regarded as an officer or employee of the company for this purpose`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the person is regarded as an officer or employee is not known
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person may not be appointed as an independent assessor— (a) if he is— ... (b) if he is— ... (c) if there exists between— ... a connection of any such description as may be specified by regulations" -- MARGINAL a

-- ---- s 345 Meaning of "associate" ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4438 | (1) This section defines “associate” for the purposes of section 344 (independence requirement).
@ref s 345(1) Meaning of "associate": the purposes (src:4438)
GIVEN `the purpose is section 344 (independence requirement)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 345(1) this section defines "associate" for the purposes` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is section 344 (independence requirement)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section defines “associate” for the purposes of section 344 (independence requirement)"

-- (6) "in relation to a limited liability partnership, for “director” read “member”": whether the person counts as a director.
-- src:4452 | (6) In this section, in relation to a limited liability partnership, for “director” read “member”.
@ref s 345(6) Meaning of "associate": limited liability partnerships (src:4452)
GIVEN `the body corporate is a limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 345(6) the person counts as a director of the body corporate for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the body corporate is a limited liability partnership`
    THEN `the person is a member of the body corporate`
    ELSE `the person is a director of the body corporate`

-- src:4439 | (2) In relation to an individual, “associate” means—
-- src:4440 | (a) that individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child,
-- src:4441 | (b) any body corporate of which that individual is a director, and
-- src:4442 | (c) any employee or partner of that individual.
@ref s 345(2) Meaning of "associate": an individual (src:4439-4442)
GIVEN `the person is the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a body corporate of which the individual counts as a director (s 345(6))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee or partner of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 345(2) the person is an associate of the individual` MEANS
    IF `the person is the individual's spouse or civil partner or minor child or step-child`
        OR `the person is a body corporate of which the individual counts as a director (s 345(6))`
        OR `the person is an employee or partner of the individual`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to an individual, “associate” means— (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..."

-- src:4443 | (3) In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means—
-- src:4444 | (a) any body corporate of which that body is a director,
-- src:4445 | (b) any body corporate in the same group as that body, and
-- src:4446 | (c) any employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group.
@ref s 345(3) Meaning of "associate": a body corporate (src:4443-4446)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate of which that body counts as a director (s 345(6))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a body corporate in the same group as that body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 345(3) the person is an associate of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the person is a body corporate of which that body counts as a director (s 345(6))`
        OR `the person is a body corporate in the same group as that body`
        OR `the person is an employee or partner of that body or of any body corporate in the same group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a body corporate, “associate” means— (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..."

-- src:4447 | (4) In relation to a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means—
-- src:4448 | (a) any body corporate of which that partnership is a director,
-- src:4449 | (b) any employee of or partner in that partnership, and
-- src:4450 | (c) any person who is an associate of a partner in that partnership.
@ref s 345(4) Meaning of "associate": a partnership that is a legal person (src:4447-4450)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate of which that partnership counts as a director (s 345(6))` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of or partner in that partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an associate of a partner in that partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 345(4) the person is an associate of the partnership` MEANS
    IF `the person is a body corporate of which that partnership counts as a director (s 345(6))`
        OR `the person is an employee of or partner in that partnership`
        OR `the person is an associate of a partner in that partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a partnership that is a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means— (a) ... (b) ... and (c) ..."

-- src:4451 | (5) In relation to a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners.
@ref s 345(5) Meaning of "associate": a partnership that is not a legal person (src:4451)
GIVEN `the person is an associate of any of the partners` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 345(5) the person is an associate of the partnership` MEANS
    IF `the person is an associate of any of the partners`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In relation to a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed, “associate” means any person who is an associate of any of the partners"

-- ---- s 346 Effect of appointment of a partnership -----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4454 | (1) This section applies where a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as an independent assessor.
@ref s 346(1) Effect of appointment of a partnership: application (src:4454)
GIVEN `a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as independent assessor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(1) this section applies to the appointment` MEANS
    IF `a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as independent assessor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as an independent assessor" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4455 | (2) Unless a contrary intention appears, the appointment is of the partnership as such and not of the partners.
@ref s 346(2) Effect of appointment of a partnership: the partnership as such (src:4455)
GIVEN `a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as independent assessor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(2) the appointment is of the partnership as such and not of the partners` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as independent assessor`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where a partnership that is not a legal person under the law by which it is governed is appointed as an independent assessor"
    ELSE IF `a contrary intention appears`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless a contrary intention appears, the appointment is of the partnership as such and not of the partners" -- FORK F15
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4460 | (a) a partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of another partnership only if the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership, and
-- src:4461 | (b) a partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership only if it or he succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership.
@ref s 346(4) Effect of appointment of a partnership: succession (src:4460-4461)
GIVEN `the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(4)(a) the partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` MEANS
    IF `the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership` AND `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of another partnership only if the members of the successor partnership are substantially the same as those of the former partnership" -- FORK F16

@ref s 346(4)(b) Effect of appointment of a partnership: succession by a person (src:4461)
GIVEN `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(4)(b) the partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership` MEANS
    IF `the successor succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership only if it or he succeeds to the whole or substantially the whole of the business of the former partnership"

DECLARE `s 346(3) successor` IS ONE OF
    `s 346(3)(a) a partnership that succeeds to the practice of that partnership`
    `s 346(3)(b) any other person who succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership`

-- src:4456 | (3) Where the partnership ceases, the appointment is to be treated as extending to—
-- src:4457 | (a) any partnership that succeeds to the practice of that partnership, or
-- src:4458 | (b) any other person who succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership.
@ref s 346(3) Effect of appointment of a partnership: where the partnership ceases (src:4456-4458)
GIVEN `the partnership ceases` IS A BOOLEAN
      successor IS A `s 346(3) successor`
      `s 346(4)(a) the partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 346(4)(b) the partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(3) the appointment is treated as extending to the successor` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the partnership ceases`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the partnership ceases, the appointment is to be treated as extending to—" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE CONSIDER successor
         WHEN `s 346(3)(a) a partnership that succeeds to the practice of that partnership` THEN `s 346(4)(a) the partnership is regarded as succeeding to the practice of the former partnership`
         WHEN `s 346(3)(b) any other person who succeeds to that practice having previously carried it on in partnership` THEN `s 346(4)(b) the partnership or other person is regarded as succeeding to the practice of a partnership`

-- src:4462 | (5) Where the partnership ceases and the appointment is not treated under subsection (3) as extending to any partnership or other person, the appointment may with the consent of the company be treated as extending to a partnership, or other person, who succeeds to—
-- src:4463 | (a) the business of the former partnership, or
-- src:4464 | (b) such part of it as is agreed by the company is to be treated as comprising the appointment.
@ref s 346(5) Effect of appointment of a partnership: consent of the company (src:4462-4464)
GIVEN `the partnership ceases and the appointment is not treated under subsection (3) as extending to any partnership or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the successor succeeds to the business of the former partnership or to such part of it as the company agrees is to be treated as comprising the appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 346(5) the appointment may be treated as extending to the successor` MEANS
    IF `the partnership ceases and the appointment is not treated under subsection (3) as extending to any partnership or other person`
        AND `the company consents`
        AND `the successor succeeds to the business of the former partnership or to such part of it as the company agrees is to be treated as comprising the appointment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the appointment may with the consent of the company be treated as extending to a partnership, or other person, who succeeds to— (a) the business of the former partnership, or (b) such part of it as is agreed by the company"

-- ---- s 347 The independent assessor's report ----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4466 | (1) The report of the independent assessor must state his opinion whether—
-- src:4467 | (a) the procedures adopted in connection with the poll or polls were adequate;
-- src:4468 | (b) the votes cast (including proxy votes) were fairly and accurately recorded and counted;
-- src:4469 | (c) the validity of members' appointments of proxies was fairly assessed;
-- src:4470 | (d) the notice of the meeting complied with section 325 (notice of meeting to contain statement of rights to appoint proxy);
-- src:4471 | (e) section 326 (company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies) was complied with in relation to the meeting.
@ref s 347(1) The independent assessor's report: the opinions (src:4466-4471)
GIVEN `the report states his opinion whether the procedures adopted in connection with the poll or polls were adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states his opinion whether the votes cast (including proxy votes) were fairly and accurately recorded and counted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states his opinion whether the validity of members' appointments of proxies was fairly assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states his opinion whether the notice of the meeting complied with section 325` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report states his opinion whether section 326 was complied with in relation to the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(1) the report states the opinions this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the report states his opinion whether the procedures adopted in connection with the poll or polls were adequate`
        AND `the report states his opinion whether the votes cast (including proxy votes) were fairly and accurately recorded and counted`
        AND `the report states his opinion whether the validity of members' appointments of proxies was fairly assessed`
        AND `the report states his opinion whether the notice of the meeting complied with section 325`
        AND `the report states his opinion whether section 326 was complied with in relation to the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report of the independent assessor must state his opinion whether— (a) ... (e) section 326 (company-sponsored invitations to appoint proxies) was complied with in relation to the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4472 | (2) The report must give his reasons for the opinions stated.
@ref s 347(2) The independent assessor's report: reasons (src:4472)
GIVEN `the report gives his reasons for the opinions stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(2) the report gives the reasons this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the report gives his reasons for the opinions stated`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must give his reasons for the opinions stated" -- FORK F5

-- src:4473 | (3) If he is unable to form an opinion on any of those matters, the report must record that fact and state the reasons for it.
@ref s 347(3) The independent assessor's report: unable to form an opinion (src:4473)
GIVEN `he is unable to form an opinion on any of those matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report records that fact and states the reasons for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(3) the report records that he is unable to form an opinion and states the reasons` MEANS
    IF (NOT `he is unable to form an opinion on any of those matters`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If he is unable to form an opinion on any of those matters" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `the report records that fact and states the reasons for it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the report must record that fact and state the reasons for it" -- FORK F5

-- src:4474 | (4) The report must state the name of the independent assessor.
@ref s 347(4) The independent assessor's report: the name (src:4474)
GIVEN `the report states the name of the independent assessor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(4) the report states the name of the independent assessor` MEANS
    IF `the report states the name of the independent assessor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The report must state the name of the independent assessor" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 348 Rights of independent assessor: right to attend meeting etc -------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 348(1) occasion` IS ONE OF
    `s 348(1)(a) the meeting at which the poll may be taken`
    `s 348(1)(b) any subsequent proceedings in connection with the poll`
    `s 348(1) another occasion`

-- src:4476 | (1) Where an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll, he is entitled to attend—
-- src:4477 | (a) the meeting at which the poll may be taken, and
-- src:4478 | (b) any subsequent proceedings in connection with the poll.
@ref s 348(1) Rights of independent assessor: right to attend (src:4476-4478)
GIVEN `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on the poll` IS A BOOLEAN
      occasion IS A `s 348(1) occasion`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 348(1) the independent assessor is entitled to attend` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on the poll`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll, he is entitled to attend"
    ELSE CONSIDER occasion
         WHEN `s 348(1) another occasion` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "he is entitled to attend— (a) the meeting at which the poll may be taken, and (b) any subsequent proceedings in connection with the poll"
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 348(2) document` IS ONE OF
    `s 348(2)(a) the notice of the meeting`
    `s 348(2)(b) any other communication provided by the company in connection with the meeting to persons who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates`
    `s 348(2) another document`

-- src:4479 | (2) He is also entitled to be provided by the company with a copy of—
-- src:4480 | (a) the notice of the meeting, and
-- src:4481 | (b) any other communication provided by the company in connection with the meeting to persons who have a right to vote on the matter to which the poll relates.
