    IF (NOT `the statement was made in response to a requirement under this section`) OR (NOT `the proceedings are criminal proceedings`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under this section may not be used in evidence against him in criminal proceedings"
    ELSE IF `the proceedings are for an offence under section 350 (offences relating to provision of information)`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the exception removes the bar; it does not say the statement may be used -- FORK F17
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be used in evidence against him in criminal proceedings except proceedings for an offence under section 350"

