    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is not required by this section to disclose information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege (in Scotland, to confidentiality of communications) could be maintained in legal proceedings"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information in respect of which a claim to legal professional privilege ... could be maintained"

