-- src:4499 | (1) A person who fails to comply with a requirement under section 349 without delay commits an offence unless it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanation.
@ref s 350(1) Offences relating to provision of information: failing to comply (src:4499)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply without delay with a requirement under section 349` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person fails to comply without delay with a requirement under section 349`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who fails to comply with a requirement under section 349 without delay commits an offence" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanation`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "commits an offence unless it was not reasonably practicable for him to provide the required information or explanation" -- FORK F8
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4500 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 350(2) Offences relating to provision of information: penalty for failing to comply (src:4500)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 350(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- src:4501 | (3) A person commits an offence who knowingly or recklessly makes to an independent assessor a statement (oral or written) that—
-- src:4502 | (a) conveys or purports to convey any information or explanations which the independent assessor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 349, and
-- src:4503 | (b) is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 350(3) Offences relating to provision of information: false or misleading statement (src:4501-4503)
GIVEN `the person knowingly or recklessly makes to an independent assessor a statement (oral or written)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement conveys or purports to convey information or explanations which the independent assessor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 349` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350(3) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly or recklessly makes to an independent assessor a statement (oral or written)`
        AND `the statement conveys or purports to convey information or explanations which the independent assessor requires, or is entitled to require, under section 349`
        AND `the statement is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence who knowingly or recklessly makes to an independent assessor a statement (oral or written) that— (a) ... and (b) is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular" -- MARGINAL a

-- (4): on indictment, imprisonment not exceeding two years or a fine (or both); on summary conviction in England and Wales,
-- imprisonment not exceeding twelve months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both); in Scotland or Northern
-- Ireland, imprisonment not exceeding six months or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
-- src:4504 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable—
-- src:4505 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:4506 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:4507 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:4508 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 350(4) Offences relating to provision of information: penalty for a false statement (src:4504-4508)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 350(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) on summary conviction— (i) in England and Wales ... (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland": the place of conviction is not stated

-- src:4509 | (5) Nothing in this section affects any right of an independent assessor to apply for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 348 or 349.
@ref s 350(5) Offences relating to provision of information: injunction (src:4509)
GIVEN `the assessor applies for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 348 or 349` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 350(5) this section affects the assessor's right to apply for the injunction` MEANS
    IF `the assessor applies for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 348 or 349`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects any right of an independent assessor to apply for an injunction"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any right of an independent assessor to apply for an injunction (in Scotland, an interdict or an order for specific performance) to enforce any of his rights under section 348 or 349"

-- ---- s 351 Information to be made available on website -------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4511 | (1) Where an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll, the company must ensure that the following information is made available on a website—
-- src:4512 | (a) the fact of his appointment,
-- src:4513 | (b) his identity,
-- src:4514 | (c) the text of the resolution or, as the case may be, a description of the subject matter of the poll to which his appointment relates, and
-- src:4515 | (d) a copy of a report by him which complies with section 347.
@ref s 351(1) Information to be made available on website (src:4511-4515)
GIVEN `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fact of his appointment is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `his identity is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll to which his appointment relates is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of a report by him which complies with section 347 is made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(1) the company has made the information available on a website` MEANS
    IF (NOT `an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an independent assessor has been appointed to report on a poll"
    ELSE IF `the fact of his appointment is made available on a website`
            AND `his identity is made available on a website`
            AND `the text of the resolution or a description of the subject matter of the poll to which his appointment relates is made available on a website`
            AND `a copy of a report by him which complies with section 347 is made available on a website`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must ensure that the following information is made available on a website— (a) the fact of his appointment, (b) his identity, (c) the text of the resolution ..., and (d) a copy of a report by him which complies with section 347" -- FORK F5

-- src:4516 | (2) The provisions of section 353 (requirements as to website availability) apply.
@ref s 351(2) Information to be made available on website: section 353 (src:4516)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of section 353` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(2) the provision of section 353 applies for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a provision of section 353`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The provisions of section 353 (requirements as to website availability) apply"

-- src:4517 | (3) In the event of default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section), an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 351(3) Information to be made available on website: offence (src:4517)
GIVEN `the company is in default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(3) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company is in default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section)`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the event of default in complying with this section (or with the requirements of section 353 as it applies for the purposes of this section), an offence is committed b ..." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4518 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 351(4) Information to be made available on website: penalty (src:4518)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 351(4) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
-- src:4519 | (5) Failure to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353) does not affect the validity of—
-- src:4520 | (a) the poll, or
-- src:4521 | (b) the resolution or other business (if passed or agreed to) to which the poll relates.
@ref s 351(5) Information to be made available on website: validity (src:4519-4521)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 351(5) the failure affects the validity of the poll or of the resolution or other business to which the poll relates` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section (or the requirements of section 353) does not affect the validity of— (a) the poll, or (b) the resolution or other business (if passed ..."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply

§§ `Supplementary`

-- ---- s 352 Application of provisions to class meetings ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4524 | (1) The provisions of section 341 (results of poll to be made available on website) apply (with any necessary modifications) in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares of a quoted company or traded company in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares as they apply in relation to a general meeting of the company.
@ref s 352(1) Application of provisions to class meetings: section 341 (src:4524)
GIVEN `the company is a quoted company or a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 352(1) section 341 applies (with any necessary modifications) to the class meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company is a quoted company or a traded company` AND `the meeting is a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a meeting of holders of a class of shares of a quoted company or traded company in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares"

-- src:4525 | (1A) The provisions of section 342 to 351 (independent report on poll) apply (with any necessary modifications) in relation to a meeting of holders of a class of shares of a quoted company in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares as they apply in relation to a general meeting of the company.
@ref s 352(1A) Application of provisions to class meetings: sections 342 to 351 (src:4525)
GIVEN `s 361 the company is a quoted company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 352(1A) sections 342 to 351 apply (with any necessary modifications) to the class meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the meeting is a meeting of holders of a class of shares in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with the variation of the rights attached to such shares"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 361 the company is a quoted company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a meeting of holders of a class of shares of a quoted company"

DECLARE `s 352(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 352(2)(a) any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles`
    `s 352(2)(b) the abrogation of rights attached to a class of shares`
    `s 352(2) another act`

-- src:4526 | (2) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:4527 | (a) any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles, is itself to be treated as a variation of those rights, and
-- src:4528 | (b) references to the variation of rights attached to a class of shares include references to their abrogation.
@ref s 352(2) Application of provisions to class meetings: what is a variation (src:4526-4528)
GIVEN act IS A `s 352(2) act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 352(2) the act is treated as a variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 352(2) another act` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "references to the variation of rights attached to a class of shares include references to their abrogation"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 353 Requirements as to website availability ---------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4530 | (1) The following provisions apply for the purposes of—
-- src:4531 | section 341 (results of poll to be made available on website), and
-- src:4532 | section 351 (report of independent observer to be made available on website).
@ref s 353(1) Requirements as to website availability: the sections (src:4530-4532)
GIVEN section IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(1) the following provisions apply for the purposes of the section` MEANS
    IF section EQUALS "341" OR section EQUALS "351"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The following provisions apply for the purposes of— section 341 ... and section 351"

-- src:4533 | (2) The information must be made available on a website that—
-- src:4534 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:4535 | (b) identifies the company in question.
@ref s 353(2) Requirements as to website availability: the website (src:4533-4535)
GIVEN `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(2) the website is one this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information must be made available on a website that— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company in question" -- FORK F5

-- src:4536 | (3) Access to the information on the website, and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the information from the website, must not be conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 353(3) Requirements as to website availability: no fee (src:4536)
GIVEN `access to the information, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(3) access to the information is as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `access to the information, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Access to the information on the website, and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the information from the website, must not be conditional on the payment of a fee or otherwise restricted"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4538 | (a) must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable, and
@ref s 353(4)(a) Requirements as to website availability: as soon as reasonably practicable (src:4538)
GIVEN `the information was made available as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(4)(a) the information was made available in time` MEANS
    IF `the information was made available as soon as reasonably practicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information— (a) must be made available as soon as reasonably practicable" -- FORK F5

-- "throughout the period of two years beginning with the date on which it is first made available": the period ends on the
-- day before the second anniversary of that date.
-- src:4539 | (b) must be kept available throughout the period of two years beginning with the date on which it is first made available on a website in accordance with this section.
@ref s 353(4)(b) Requirements as to website availability: kept available for two years (src:4539)
GIVEN `the date on which the information was first made available on a website` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the information was kept available` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(4)(b) the information was kept available throughout the two years` MEANS
    IF `the last day on which the information was kept available` AT LEAST (`add years` `the date on which the information was first made available on a website` 2) MINUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available throughout the period of two years beginning with the date on which it is first made available on a website" -- FORK F7

-- src:4540 | (5) A failure to make information available on a website throughout the period specified in subsection (4)(b) is disregarded if—
-- src:4541 | (a) the information is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:4542 | (b) the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 353(5) Requirements as to website availability: a failure disregarded (src:4540-4542)
GIVEN `the information is made available on the website for part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 353(5) the failure to make the information available throughout the period is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the information is made available on the website for part of the period`
        AND `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A failure to make information available on a website throughout the period specified in subsection (4)(b) is disregarded if" -- MARGINAL a

-- s 354 Power to limit or extend the types of company to which provisions of this Chapter apply (ss 354(1) to (4)):
-- regulation-making power of the Secretary of State and the procedure for the regulations; machinery (inert, reason 2).
